{"id":"reserve-code-how-computer-scientist-larry","date":"2026-10-21","topic":"code","region":"americas","headline":"How computer scientist Larry Tesler created copy and paste","source":{"name":"Wikipedia","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Larry_Tesler"},"accent":"us","tiers":{"t1":{"sentences":[{"text":"Larry Tesler worked on early computers in America.","voice":null,"roles":["S","S","V","M","M","M","M","M"],"dur":null,"voiceJa":null,"durJa":null},{"text":"He made a simple way to move screen text.","voice":null,"roles":["S","V","O","O","O","O","O","O","O"],"dur":null,"voiceJa":null,"durJa":null},{"text":"Larry worked with Tim Mott to help computer users.","voice":null,"roles":["S","V","M","M","M","M","M","M","M"],"dur":null,"voiceJa":null,"durJa":null},{"text":"He did not like hard states in computer software.","voice":null,"roles":["S","V","V","V","O","O","M","M","M"],"dur":null,"voiceJa":null,"durJa":null},{"text":"His personal car had a sign with no modes.","voice":null,"roles":["S","S","S","V","O","O","O","O","O"],"dur":null,"voiceJa":null,"durJa":null}],"bands":{"core1000":85,"core1800":8,"ngsl":2,"tsl":0,"nawl":0,"beyond":5},"grammar":[{"i":1,"focus":"to move screen text","title":"Infinitive Phrase as Adjective","note":"The infinitive phrase 'to move screen text' acts as an adjective modifying 'way'. It clarifies what kind of method or action was made."},{"i":3,"focus":"did not like","title":"Simple Past Negative","note":"To form a negative sentence in simple past tense, use 'did not' followed by the base form 'like'. It expresses a negative situation or state in the past."}]},"t2":{"sentences":[{"text":"Computer scientist Larry Tesler created easy ways to handle text.","voice":null,"roles":["S","S","S","S","V","O","O","O","O","O"],"dur":null,"voiceJa":null,"durJa":null},{"text":"He worked at Xerox PARC and Apple during his career.","voice":null,"roles":["S","V","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M"],"dur":null,"voiceJa":null,"durJa":null},{"text":"Tesler and Tim Mott created the basic copy and paste commands.","voice":null,"roles":["S","S","S","S","V","O","O","O","O","O","O"],"dur":null,"voiceJa":null,"durJa":null},{"text":"These tools helped people copy words without typing them again.","voice":null,"roles":["S","S","V","O","C","C","M","M","M","M"],"dur":null,"voiceJa":null,"durJa":null},{"text":"He disliked software modes because they trapped users in single actions.","voice":null,"roles":["S","V","O","O","M","S","V","O","M","M","M"],"dur":null,"voiceJa":null,"durJa":null},{"text":"So he put the words NO MODES on his car license plate.","voice":null,"roles":["M","S","V","O","O","O","O","M","M","M","M","M"],"dur":null,"voiceJa":null,"durJa":null}],"bands":{"core1000":70,"core1800":20,"ngsl":4,"tsl":2,"nawl":0,"beyond":4},"grammar":[{"i":3,"focus":"helped people copy","title":"Bare Infinitive After Help","note":"The verb 'help' can take an object and a bare infinitive without 'to'. Here, 'copy' acts as a complement describing the action done by 'people'."},{"i":4,"focus":"because they trapped users in single actions","title":"Adverbial Clause of Reason","note":"The conjunction 'because' introduces a subordinate clause explaining why Tesler disliked software modes. It links cause and effect clearly across two clauses."}]},"t3":{"sentences":[{"text":"Computer scientist Larry Tesler has created software tools that millions of people use daily.","voice":null,"roles":["S","S","S","S","V","V","O","O","O","S","S","S","V","M"],"dur":null,"voiceJa":null,"durJa":null},{"text":"While working at Xerox PARC, he collaborated with Tim Mott on digital document features.","voice":null,"roles":["M","M","M","M","M","S","V","M","M","M","M","M","M","M"],"dur":null,"voiceJa":null,"durJa":null},{"text":"They invented cut, copy, and paste to simplify moving text across computer screens.","voice":null,"roles":["S","V","O","O","O","O","M","M","M","M","M","M","M"],"dur":null,"voiceJa":null,"durJa":null},{"text":"Tesler later moved to Apple, where he helped develop software for personal computers.","voice":null,"roles":["S","M","V","M","M","M","S","V","C","C","C","C","C"],"dur":null,"voiceJa":null,"durJa":null},{"text":"He strongly opposed software modes, which limit user actions to specific fixed states.","voice":null,"roles":["S","M","V","O","O","S","V","O","O","M","M","M","M"],"dur":null,"voiceJa":null,"durJa":null},{"text":"He disliked these restrictions so much that he put a message on his car.","voice":null,"roles":["S","V","O","O","M","M","M","S","V","O","O","M","M","M"],"dur":null,"voiceJa":null,"durJa":null},{"text":"His personal license plate proudly displayed the words NO MODES to promote his philosophy.","voice":null,"roles":["S","S","S","S","M","V","O","O","O","O","M","M","M","M"],"dur":null,"voiceJa":null,"durJa":null}],"bands":{"core1000":70,"core1800":16,"ngsl":7,"tsl":2,"nawl":0,"beyond":5},"grammar":[{"i":0,"focus":"has created","title":"Present Perfect Tense","note":"The present perfect 'has created' shows an action completed in the past that remains important today. It connects past invention with ongoing current usage."},{"i":4,"focus":", which limit user actions to specific fixed states","title":"Non-defining Relative Clause","note":"Introduced by ', which', this relative clause adds supplementary explanation about 'software modes'. Non-defining clauses are offset with commas and can be removed without changing the core meaning."}]},"t4":{"sentences":[{"text":"American computer scientist Larry Tesler made fundamental contributions to early user interface design throughout his long career.","voice":null,"roles":["S","S","S","S","S","V","O","O","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M"],"dur":null,"voiceJa":null,"durJa":null},{"text":"While employed at Xerox PARC, he collaborated with Tim Mott to create essential document editing functions.","voice":null,"roles":["M","M","M","M","M","S","V","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M"],"dur":null,"voiceJa":null,"durJa":null},{"text":"The pair introduced cut, copy, and paste, which allowed text to be duplicated easily without rewriting.","voice":null,"roles":["S","S","V","O","O","O","O","S","V","O","C","C","C","C","C","C"],"dur":null,"voiceJa":null,"durJa":null},{"text":"Tesler subsequently joined Apple, where his technical skills were applied to landmark personal computer projects.","voice":null,"roles":["S","M","V","O","M","S","S","S","V","V","M","M","M","M","M"],"dur":null,"voiceJa":null,"durJa":null},{"text":"Throughout his work, he consistently advocated for modeless software, where system commands remain accessible at all times.","voice":null,"roles":["M","M","M","S","M","V","M","M","M","M","S","S","V","C","M","M","M"],"dur":null,"voiceJa":null,"durJa":null},{"text":"He reported that restrictive operating modes created unnecessary confusion and caused frequent errors for average users.","voice":null,"roles":["S","V","M","S","S","S","V","O","O","M","V","O","O","M","M","M"],"dur":null,"voiceJa":null,"durJa":null},{"text":"To demonstrate his commitment to this design principle, his personal vehicle carried a customized license plate reading NO MODES.","voice":null,"roles":["M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","S","S","S","V","O","O","O","O","O","O","O"],"dur":null,"voiceJa":null,"durJa":null},{"text":"His user-friendly design principles have continued to influence modern operating systems across the globe.","voice":null,"roles":["S","S","S","S","V","V","O","O","O","O","O","O","O","O"],"dur":null,"voiceJa":null,"durJa":null}],"bands":{"core1000":63,"core1800":18,"ngsl":6,"tsl":5,"nawl":1,"beyond":7},"grammar":[{"i":2,"focus":"to be duplicated","title":"Passive Infinitive","note":"The passive infinitive 'to be duplicated' highlights what happens to 'text' rather than who performs the duplication. It follows the pattern 'allow + object + passive infinitive'."},{"i":3,"focus":"were applied","title":"Passive Voice in Past Tense","note":"The passive form 'were applied' focuses on 'his technical skills' as the receiver of the action. It is formed using past tense 'were' plus the past participle 'applied'."}]},"t5":{"sentences":[{"text":"Pioneering computer scientist Larry Tesler played a pivotal role in shaping modern interactive user experiences during the early decades of computing.","voice":null,"roles":["S","S","S","S","S","V","O","O","O","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M"],"dur":null,"voiceJa":null,"durJa":null},{"text":"While working at Xerox PARC in the 1970s, Tesler and his colleague Tim Mott developed the revolutionary concepts of cut, copy, and paste.","voice":null,"roles":["M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","S","S","S","S","S","S","V","O","O","O","O","O","O","O","O"],"dur":null,"voiceJa":null,"durJa":null},{"text":"These groundbreaking commands eliminated repetitive text-entry tasks, forever transforming digital document processing across emerging desktop platforms.","voice":null,"roles":["S","S","S","V","O","O","O","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M"],"dur":null,"voiceJa":null,"durJa":null},{"text":"Tesler later joined Apple, where he helped refine application programming toolkits and software interfaces for seminal personal computers.","voice":null,"roles":["S","M","V","O","M","S","V","C","C","C","C","C","C","C","C","C","C","C"],"dur":null,"voiceJa":null,"durJa":null},{"text":"Beyond his contributions to text manipulation, Tesler became an ardent defender of modeless software design.","voice":null,"roles":["M","M","M","M","M","M","S","V","C","C","C","C","C","C","C"],"dur":null,"voiceJa":null,"durJa":null},{"text":"In modeless systems, software actions remain constantly available rather than forcing users into restrictive, state-dependent operating modes.","voice":null,"roles":["M","M","M","S","S","V","M","C","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M"],"dur":null,"voiceJa":null,"durJa":null},{"text":"Tesler maintained that rigid software modes imposed unnecessary cognitive burdens on users and frequently triggered avoidable operating mistakes.","voice":null,"roles":["S","V","M","S","S","S","V","O","O","O","M","M","M","M","V","O","O","O"],"dur":null,"voiceJa":null,"durJa":null},{"text":"To express his passionate stance against modal software, he famously customized his personal automobile with a license plate displaying NO MODES.","voice":null,"roles":["M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","S","M","V","O","O","O","M","M","M","M","M","M","M"],"dur":null,"voiceJa":null,"durJa":null},{"text":"His relentless focus on intuitive computer interaction established fundamental design standards that remain ubiquitous across digital devices today.","voice":null,"roles":["S","S","S","S","S","S","S","V","O","O","O","S","V","C","M","M","M","M"],"dur":null,"voiceJa":null,"durJa":null}],"bands":{"core1000":54,"core1800":17,"ngsl":10,"tsl":3,"nawl":3,"beyond":13},"grammar":[{"i":2,"focus":"forever transforming digital document processing","title":"Participle Phrase as Result Modifier","note":"The present participle phrase 'forever transforming...' functions as an adverbial modifier describing the consequential result of the main action. It elaborates on the historical impact of eliminating repetitive tasks."},{"i":8,"focus":"that remain ubiquitous","title":"Subject Relative Clause","note":"The relative pronoun 'that' serves as the subject inside the relative clause. It introduces essential information defining the 'fundamental design standards'."}]}},"glossary":[{"word":"commands","lemma":"command","pos":"noun","ipa":"/kəˈmændz/","definition":"instructions given to a computer to perform specific tasks","tiers":["t2","t4","t5"]},{"word":"collaborated","lemma":"collaborate","pos":"verb","ipa":"/kəˈlæb.ə.reɪ.tɪd/","definition":"worked together with another person to produce something","tiers":["t3","t4"]},{"word":"modeless","lemma":"modeless","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈmoʊd.ləs/","definition":"allowing all computer actions without requiring a special operational mode","tiers":["t4","t5"]},{"word":"advocated","lemma":"advocate","pos":"verb","ipa":"/ˈæd.və.keɪ.t